--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0329 made every filtering threshold the *data paper* reports a
`{{< meta >}}` macro read from `config/corpus_filter.yaml`. The same numbers
are still typed as literals one deliverable over:

- `deliverables/_shared/_includes/corpus-filtering.md:14,25` — the reranker
  threshold `0.002`, twice, plus the Tier-3/4 concept-group rule
- `deliverables/_shared/_includes/annex-crossencoder.md:26` — `0.002` three
  times, and the superseded `0.0049`

Both includes feed `deliverables/corpus-report/corpus-report.qmd`, and that
document is the reason 0329 could not simply convert them. It reads
`../_shared/technical-report-vars.yml`, but it is **absent from
`compute_vars.DOC_VARS`**, which is keyed by document. So declaring
`filter_reranker_threshold` under `technical-report` to serve corpus-report
trips `test_doc_vars_no_extras` (the variable is unused in
`technical-report.qmd` itself), and not declaring it renders an empty macro
in corpus-report. Neither branch works without first wiring corpus-report
into the registry.

The values agree with config today, so this is drift risk rather than a live
error. It becomes an error the first time the threshold is recalibrated —
which the annex shows has already happened once, 0.0049 to 0.002.

Second, smaller gap in the same area: `test_doc_vars_completeness` maps a
document name to `deliverables/*/<name>.qmd`, so any deliverable outside
`DOC_VARS` is unguarded in both directions. corpus-report is currently the
only one, but the guard should key off the documents that exist rather than
off the registry, or the next unregistered deliverable is equally invisible.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/analysis/compute_vars.py` — `DOC_VARS`, `DOC_OUTPUT_DIR`
- `deliverables/corpus-report/corpus-report.qmd` — reads technical-report-vars.yml
- `deliverables/_shared/_includes/corpus-filtering.md`, `annex-crossencoder.md`
- `tests/test_doc_vars_completeness.py` — the registry-keyed guard
- `tests/test_handoff_artifacts_tracked.py` — the tracked-artifact coverage guard (0329)

## Actions

1. Decide the registry shape: either register corpus-report as its own
   document with its own vars file, or make `DOC_VARS` express "these
   documents share technical-report-vars.yml". Sharing is the existing
   reality, so the registry should say so rather than the render doing it
   implicitly through `metadata-files`.
2. Convert the `0.002` literals in both includes to macros.
3. Widen `test_doc_vars_completeness` to discover deliverables from disk, so
   an unregistered document fails loudly instead of being skipped.

## Test

- Red first: a guard asserting no `_includes/*.md` hand-types a value that
  exists in `config/corpus_filter.yaml`, failing today on `0.002`.

## Verification

- [ ] corpus-report renders with no empty macros
- [ ] Changing `reranker_threshold` in config changes both deliverables
- [ ] A deliverable absent from DOC_VARS fails the completeness guard

## Invariants

- The historical `0.0049` in the annex is a *superseded* value being narrated,
  not the current threshold — it must stay a literal, not become a macro.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every live threshold in the corpus report traces to config
